45	     *
46	     * <p>A pushed summary is the one piece of client input that outlives its request: it lands in the
47	     * {@code summaries} table, and every cross-session endpoint ({@code /api/insights}, {@code
48	     * /api/eval}, {@code /api/mine}, {@code /api/optimize}) later parses up to 150 of them into
49	     * object trees at once. Without a bound, a handful of oversized documents do not merely make one
50	     * request expensive — they make every subsequent read of those endpoints fail, until the rows are
51	     * deleted by hand.
52	     *
53	     * <p>The ceiling is set above anything the server itself produces: {@link
54	     * AnalysisOrchestrator#normalize} bounds a model's analysis to roughly 120 KB of text in the
55	     * worst case, so 256 KiB leaves generous headroom while keeping the aggregate of 150 summaries
56	     * to a size the heap can hold.
57	     */
58	    static final int MAX_SUMMARY_CHARS = 256 * 1024;
59	
